        "title": "19th Century: Darwin, Marx, Nietzsche",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The 19th century produced three ideas that shattered the intellectual foundations of the\nEnlightenment world: Darwin's evolution (humans are animals, shaped by natural selection),\nMarx's historical materialism (ideas are products of material conditions, history is class\nstruggle), and Nietzsche's critique of values (God is dead, morality is will to power).\nTogether they are the intellectual roots of modernity and its discontents."
    }
